  "_commit": {
    "id": "8913bb81aa5d06efff77c96434d27bc788eec106",
    "author": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "committer": "EllisPatrick <ellis.patrick@sydney.edu.au>",
    "message": "1.15.1: kontextualTest() (Kontextual between conditions or with survival); SpatioMark in C++\n\n- kontextualTest(cells, parentDf, condition, r): every triple of a parentDf, tested between conditions\n  or against survival with patients as the units. Each image's Kontextual statistic is compared with\n  its exact expectation and variance when the `to` cells are a random choice among the parent's cells,\n  so a change in tissue composition does not by itself look like a change in the relationship; images\n  are combined by a frailty GEE with a CR2 variance. Computed by spicyR::kontextualEngine() (spicyR >=\n  1.99.3, now imported). The vignette's survival analysis uses it instead of spicy(alternateResult = ).\n- getDistances(), getAbundances(): a grid search in C++ (src/neighbours.cpp) replaces closepairs() and\n  pivot_wider(); identical values (6.8 s -> 1.1 s on kerenSCE). Columns in order of first appearance.\n- calcStateChanges(): every marker and distance (abundance) column of a group fitted at once by least\n  squares (Frisch-Waugh-Lovell); identical to lmFit apart from rounding-noise rows of markers that do\n  not vary within a group; 3-5x faster. test = \"nb\" and missing intensities use the previous code.\n- kerenSCE re-saved with updateObject() (identical content; reducedDim<- 1.3 s -> 0.02 s).\n- Tests against closepairs()/pivot_wider() and lmFit. R CMD check: 2 NOTEs, BiocCheck: 0 errors and\n  2 warnings, all present before these changes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01565yM83d4hBtPbzno6i5Fo\n",
    "time": 1791026012
  },
